{
  "dom_id": "step-q336006",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(1<X\\le 3).$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{7}{20}$ | $\\frac{11}{20}$ | $\\frac{17}{20}$ | $1$ |\n\n$P(1<X\\le 3)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo compute the probability of a random variable $X$ over an interval, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)=F(b)-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X\\le 3) & =F(3)-F(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{20}-\\frac{7}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
